    "summary": "When a reviewer's report contradicts its empty comments array, the fallback posts its whole event buffer, not the report text reportText found. Exploration bullets become findings, and the JSON line can be posted raw.",
    "failure_scenario": "A reviewer narrates \"I'll check:\\n- retry.go\\n- auth.go\", makes tool calls, writes \"- [high] foo.go:3 bug\" plus `{\"comments\":[]}`, then runs one more tool call and prints a short closing line. reportText finds the report by its JSON line and sees the contradiction, so the run is marked unstructured. combinedReviewNarratives then splits the full joinAssistantText output, where the JSON is no longer last, so splitTrailJSON leaves it in. The trail gets \"- retry.go\" and \"- auth.go\" as findings and the raw JSON inside the prose."
