    "summary": "buildEventLines runs stripTrailJSON on every text block each time the detail view refreshes, which happens on every streamed Pi delta. The work grows quadratically over a long run.",
    "failure_scenario": "refreshDetailContent calls buildEventLines over the whole buffer for each new event. Pi now emits many small delta events, and each rebuild re-joins all text and runs a backward JSON scan of up to 200 lines over each block. On a long Pi review with the detail view open, CPU use grows with the square of the event count. Caching the stripped text per finished block, or stripping only the last block, avoids this."
